<$fill $name="body">

!! Does this slow down large outlines?

Untyped nodes cost a single `has[kind.type]` test and render nothing extra. Typed nodes render one small pill; the full field bar is rendered lazily, only when you expand a node. The assign dialog is rendered once globally, never per node.

!! Will it break when Streams updates?

kind-streams overrides one Streams template (`stream-row-body`), which is a stable one-liner. If a future Streams version changes that template meaningfully, update this plugin's copy to match. The override wins by `plugin-priority`, independent of Streams' version.

!! I don't see any pills.

Check that: the node actually has a `kind.type` field; the enable toggle is on (`$:/config/rimir/kind-streams/enable`); and both kind and Streams are installed. Remember a server restart is needed after installing or editing the plugin.

!! Can a stream node be a full kind instance?

Yes — a typed node is a normal kind instance (a tiddler with `kind.type` and no `kind.fields`). It participates in kind's validator, graph, and cascade-palette surfaces like any other instance.

!! How do I remove a type?

Right-click → ''Kind type…'' → ''✕ Remove type'' in the dialog (or use the type pill inside the expanded bar).

